; The questions put to the component bank, kept apart from it (wish 12).
;
; Two of these are `never` properties, and they are the first in this repository
; — the modality cross-check announced that branch as unexercised on every run
; until this scenario arrived.

(load "stdlib.pol")

(property realisable "some architecture fills every stage of the brief"
  (possible (is cur.at done)))

(property no-dead-end "no early choice can strand the design half-built"
  (live (is cur.at done)))

; THE CROSS-CUTTING LAW, and the one the brief does not state.
; "Re-runnable classification" means re-reading the text. Where the extract
; stage throws its output away, a re-run silently re-processes the whole corpus
; — so a stack that satisfies every stated requirement can still be the wrong
; answer. This FAILS, and the witness names the offending part.
(property rerun-is-affordable "re-runnable classification implies persisted text"
  (never (and (defined classify.chosen)
              (not (is extract.chosen.persists yes)))))

(property crm-stays-loose "the existing CRM is never coupled at the database"
  (never (is surface.chosen direct-db)))

; Which stages have been decided. NOTE what this query CANNOT be: writing
; `(where (k cap) (c comp)) (is k.chosen c)` to read off WHICH part fills each
; stage answers empty, in silence — the right of `is` is a literal or a chain,
; never a variable to bind (§10.2). Reading a mutable cell is the rules engine's
; job, via `holds`; see `blueprint` in arch.rules.
(query filled
  (where (k cap))
  (defined k.chosen))
